A table column is constrained only by the cells that span it alone,
and the width a spanning cell needs beyond its columns’ max-content
sizes goes to the spanned columns that aren’t constrained. Blink does
the same: ComputeSectionInlineConstraints() merges only colspan-1 cells
into a column’s constraint, and DistributeColspanCellToColumnsAuto()
hands the rest to DistributeInlineSizeToComputedInlineSizeAuto(),
whose kAboveMax case grows only the auto columns. Gecko’s
BasicTableLayoutStrategy::DistributeISizeToColumns() does too: In its
FLEX_FLEX_LARGE case, only columns with neither a percentage nor a
specified width (GetHasSpecifiedCoord()) take the extra width.
